23:07.520 --> 23:10.300
Human memory is a reconstructive repair process.

23:10.300 --> 23:13.320
I'm literally making it up, but within guardrails.

23:13.320 --> 23:23.320
You are taking present-day traces neurological residues, applying constraints based on your general knowledge of the world, and actively attempting to repair a degraded historical distinction.

23:23.940 --> 23:26.320
When you remember, you are literally reconstructing.

23:27.120 --> 23:29.120
Which explains false memories perfectly.

23:29.320 --> 23:30.120
Yes, it does.

